{start_of_verse: Intro}
[Dm] [Ab] [D/A] [D/A] [Db]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
G7     |G6     |Cm     |G      |x2 (with riff 1)
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The [G7]breath of the morning [G6]I keep forgetting
the [Cm/G]smell of the warm summer air[G]
I [G7]live in a town where you [G6]can't smell a thing,
[Cm/G]you watch your feet for [G]cracks in the [G7]pave-ment.[G6][Cm/G][G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: With Riff 1}
Up above aliens hover
making home movies for the folks back home,
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Of all these weird creatures who lock up their spirits,
drill holes in themselves and live for their secrets. (with riff 2)
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Instrumental}
[A] [G] [F] [C] [E] [D] [C] [G] [G] [Gsus4] [G] [Gsus4]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
(They're all) uptight, uptight,
Uptight, uptight, Uptight,
Uptight, uptight, Uptight,
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
G7  |G6  |Cm/G  |G  |x2 (with riff 3)
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
I wish that they'd swoop down in a country lane
late at night when I'm driving.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 7}
Take me on board their beautiful ship,
show me the world as I'd love to see it.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 8}
G7  |G6  |Cm/G  |G  |x2 (with riff 4) B->G B->G
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 9}
I'd tell all my friends but they'd never believe me,
they'd think that I'd finally lost it completely.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 10}
I'd show them the stars and the meaning of life,
No time
they'd shut me away. but I'd be alright, alright,...... (with riff 1)
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 11}
Chorus (I’m Just) (uptight uptight x4)
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 12}
[G7]Up-tight                         [G6][Cm/G][G][G7]up-tight[G6][Cm/G][G]
{end_of_verse}

